  "notes": "Boot a Black Rose ROM from an empty NVRAM with the coin door open (public 22 released) and PinMAME's built-in mechanisms disabled; the scenario names no game. Leave the fresh-NVRAM loop with Escape and open the service menu. Go to the L-4 ROM's fourteenth test, T.14 CANNON TEST (after its T.12 FLIPPER COIL TEST and T.13 ORDERED LAMP, which the manual's test list predates). The manual says it shows the cannon kicker switch as SW.35 CANNON OPEN or CLOSED and the motor as ON or OFF, toggles the motor with Enter, Up or Down, and activates the cannon kicker and left lockup coils). Frames are taken on the menu items before entering because menu names blink. Drive public 35 to 1 and back to 0 and read the legend at each level, then toggle the motor twice with Enter, recording which public outputs move, and return to the menu.",
  "version": 1,
  "watch_switches": [
    22,
    35
  ]
